Name: WinSparkle
Short Name: winsparkle
URL: https://github.com/vslavik/winsparkle
Version: 0.9.4
License: MIT
License File: LICENSE
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes

Description:
WinSparkle updates Tark on Windows (W2): once a day it reads
https://gettarka.com/appcast-windows.xml and installs a newer Tark, which must
carry an EdDSA signature made with Tark's update key. Tark builds it from the
release's source zip, WinSparkle-0.9.4-src.zip, sha256
cd77040f828dce0adcf8f0205f776238197deb24f5108bf01a3e5623b703a3b9
(windows/ci/build_winsparkle.ps1); WinSparkle.dll sits next to chrome.dll.

Local Modifications:
windows/ci/winsparkle-patches/no-openssl.patch removes the legacy DSA
signature check, so the build links no OpenSSL (the release DLL links OpenSSL
1.0.2u, end of life); LICENSE still carries WinSparkle's OpenSSL notice. The
same patch refuses an update when no public key is set, where WinSparkle would
install it unsigned.
